Six more models fine-tune on raw epochs through `NeuralFineTuneConfig`. `steegformer_large` and `steegformer_largev2` are braindecode's ST-EEGFormer-large and -largeV2 (large further pretrained on HBN children's EEG), ViT-MAEs that take 128 Hz windows of a multiple of 16 samples with each channel z-scored; they get `chs_info`, so braindecode gives each channel the slot of its name, or of the nearest 10-05 site, and a channel left without a slot is refused instead of taking slot i. largeV2 needs a braindecode that finds its slots by name. `ctnet`, `deep4net`, `eegnet` and `shallowfbcspnet` have no checkpoint: they train with `train_mode="full"` from random weights, `backend_kwargs={"pretrained": False, "seed": ...}`, at 250 Hz (EEGNet at 128 Hz), and any other train mode or pretrained weights are refused. `FoundationModelSpec.hub_repo` and `embedding_dim` are `None` for these networks.
